===Glyph origin===
{{Han etyl}}
{{liushu|i}} - three parallel strokes. Compare with {{zh-l|*一}}, one stroke meaning “one”, {{zh-l|*二}}, two strokes meaning “two”, and {{zh-l|*亖}}, four strokes meaning “four”.
{{zh-etym-triple|一|one}}. See also [[畺]]. Unrelated to [[丰]].

===Etymology===
From {{inh|zh|sit-pro|*kV-sum}}.

Pronunciation in Early Middle Chinese should be ''*srim'', but actually is ''*sam'', with a non-retroflex initial consonant. This irregular development should be due by analogy with the initial of number four in EMC, ''*sijH''.

