===Glyph origin===
{{Han etyl}}
{{liushu|i}}: short horizontal below long arc (contrast {{l|zh|上}}).

===Etymology 1===
{{etymon|zh|id=under|:der|sit-pro:*(k/g)la-k/j/t<id:to fall><unc:1>}}
From {{der|zh|sit-pro|*(k/g)la-k/j/t||to fall}} (STEDT):
* inside Sinitic, cognate with {{och-l|落|to fall, to drop}}, {{och-l|露|dew}}, {{och-l|陊|to collapse}} and {{och-l|阤|hillside, slope}};
* outside Sinitic, cognate with {{cog|lus|tla ~ tlâk||to fall}}, {{m|lus|thla ~ thlâk||to drop}}, {{cog|my|ကျ||to fall}} and {{m|my|ချ||to drop}}.

{{zh-ref|Schuessler (2007)}} instead proposed an {{der|zh|aav}} origin by comparing {{och-l|下|id=1|to descend, down, below}} to {{cog|km|tr=gra'ka|t=be low, debased}}; additionally, he suggested that Sino-Tibetan influence had possibly caused the weakening of foreign final *''-k'' to OC final *''-ʔ''. He derives the departing tone ({{zh-l|*去聲}}) pronunciation via two derivations:
* {{och-l|下|id=2|to be put down}} is an [[exopassive]] derivation ([[ibid.]]);
* {{och-l|下|id=2|to descend, to fall}} is a later, general departing tone derivative ([[ibid.]]).

