[[File:Okame_Mask_20051203.jpg|thumb|250px|{{m|ja|乙|tr=oto}}: the traditional [[Noh]] [[mask]] for the [[stock character]] of a plump, clumsy, but earnest young woman.]]

Cognate with the initial ''oto-'' in {{m|ja|劣る|tr=otoru||to be less than; to be younger than}}, {{m|ja|落とす|tr=otosu||to drop something}}.<ref name="K">{{R:Kojien}}</ref><!-- <ref name="KDJ2-oto">{{R:Nihon Kokugo Daijiten 2|弟・乙}}</ref> ← Due to a Kotobank site "upgrade", many KDJ entries are missing etym details available in other editions. ☹ --><ref name="KDJ">{{R:Kokugo Dai Jiten}}</ref> Also the first element in {{m|ja|弟|tr=otōto||younger brother}}.

First attested in the ''{{w|Kojiki}}'' of 712.<ref name="KDJ2-oto">{{R:Nihon Kokugo Daijiten 2|弟・乙}}</ref><!-- Kojiki cite appears to be semantic kanji — can we confirm in man'yōgana? 乙 not found in MYS, and all instances of 弟 are semantic... -->

This is distinct from the initial ''oto-'' in {{ja-r|乙女|おとめ}}, which can instead be traced to an earlier ''woto-'' root, cognate with {{ja-r|復つ|をつ|hist=wotu}}.

