===Definitions===
{{head|zh|hanzi}}

# {{lb|zh|Classical}} {{n-g|Particle used at the end of [[copula]]r constructions involving a [[nominal]] [[predicate]];}} to [[be]] (although not grammatically a verb)
#: {{zh-x|我 亦 人 也。|I '''am''' a person, too.|CL-L}}
#: {{zh-x|其 西 有 大 山，天下 至 高 者 也。|In the west there are great mountains, which '''are''' the tallest in the world.|CL-L}}
#* {{zh-x|君子 人 與{yú}？君子 人 也。|Is he a noble person? He '''is''' a noble person.|ref=Lunyu}}
#* {{zh-x|滕 小國 也，間 於 ^齊 ^楚。事 ^齊 乎？事 ^楚 乎？|Teng '''is''' a small kingdom, between Qi and Chu. Should we serve Qi? Or Should we serve Chu?|ref=Mencius}}
#* {{zh-x|由是 觀 之，無 惻隱 之 心，非 人 也。|From this we may see that if somebody lacks a commiserating heart, they '''are''' not a human being.|ref=Mencius}}
#* {{zh-x|萬物 雖 多，其 治 一 也。|Though the myriad things are many, their government '''is''' one.|ref=Zhuangzi}}
## {{n-g|Often used more loosely than the English copula to indicate a cause or relation.}}
##* {{zh-x|死 生，命 也，其 有 夜 旦 之 常，天 也。|Life and death '''are [matters of]''' destiny. That there is the constancy of night and dawn '''is [a matter of]''' Heaven.|ref=Zhuangzi}}
##* {{zh-x|^桀 ^紂 之 失 天下 也，失 其 民 也；失 其 民 者，失 其 心 也。|That Jie and Zhou lost the empire '''was because''' they lost their people; that they lost their people '''was because''' they lost their hearts.|ref=Mencius}}
# {{lb|zh|Classical}} {{n-g|[[topic|Topic]]-marking particle used at the end of noun phrases.}}
#: {{syn|zh|者}}
#* {{zh-x|回 也，不 愚。|Hui is not foolish.|ref=Lunyu}}
#* {{zh-x|人 之 生 也，固 若 是 芒 乎！其 我 獨 芒，而 人 亦 有 不 芒 者 乎！|'''As for''' a man's life, is it hazy like this all along? Or is it mine alone which is hazy, and there are others who are not?|ref=Zhuangzi}}
#* {{zh-x|凡 法術 之 難 行 也，不 獨 萬乘，千乘 亦 然。|Generally '''concerning''' the difficulty of carrying out the law, not only the imperial realm but kingdoms are also [faced with] this.|ref=Hanfeizi}}
## [[when]], at the [[time]] of; {{n-g|especially commonly used for temporal topics, often as {{m|zh|[[及]][[其]]……也}}.}}
##* {{zh-x|丈夫 之 冠 也，父 命 之；女子 之 嫁 也，母 命 之。|'''When''' a man is capped [at the age of twenty], his father instructs him; '''when''' a girl is married, her mother instructs her.|ref=Mencius}}
##* {{zh-x|三代 之 得 天下 也 以 仁，其 失 天下 也 以 不 仁。|'''When''' the Three Dynasties gained the empire, it was through benevolence; '''when''' they lost the empire, it was through lack of benevolence.|ref=Mencius}}
##* {{zh-x|昔者，^魯 ^昭-公 少 喪 其 母，有 慈母 良。及 其 死 也，公 弗 忍 @也。|Duke Zhao of Lu was once bereaved of his mother when he was a child, and had a foster mother who was kind. '''When''' she died, the Duke could not bear it.|ref=Liji}}
# {{lb|zh|Classical}} {{n-g|Verb phrase-final particle marking [[continuous aspect]], especially common for assertions of unchanging fact.}}
#* {{zh-x|^孟 ^武 ^伯 問：「^子路 仁 乎？」子 曰：「不 知 也。」|Meng Wu Bo asked. "Is Zilu benevolent?" The Master said, "I do not know."|ref=Lunyu}}
#* {{zh-x|當是 之 時，堅車 良馬 不 知 貴 也，刻鏤 文采 不 知 喜 也。|In that age, they did not find value in sturdy chariots and good horses; they did not find pleasure in carvings and adornments.|ref=Mozi}}
#* {{zh-x|人 皆 知 有用 之 用，而 莫 知 無用 之 用 也。|Everybody knows the use in being useful, but nobody knows the use in being useless.|ref=Zhuangzi}}
# [[also]]; [[too]]; [[as well]]; {{lb|zh|in negative sentences}} [[neither]]; [[either]]
#: {{zh-x|我 也 去 了。|I '''also''' went.}}
#: {{zh-x|我 也 是 中國人。|I am Chinese '''too'''.}}
#: {{zh-x|你 如果 不 去，我 也 不 去。|If you don't go, I won't '''either'''.}}
#: {{zh-x|我 也 沒有 看見 過 它。|I haven't seen it '''either'''.}}
# {{n-g|Used for emphasis.}}
#: {{zh-x|這 也 太 不像話 了。|This is way too outrageous.}}
## {{n-g|With object fronting.}}
##: {{zh-x|他 飯 也 不 吃，覺 也 不 睡。|(Disappointingly) he neither eats nor sleeps.}}
## {{n-g|Used in the {{m|zh|[[連]]……也……}} constructions for stronger emphasis. Interchangeable with {{zh-l|*都}}.}} [[even]]
##: {{zh-x|他 連 畜生 也 不如，連 自己 的 父母 也 不 養活。|He is no better than an animal, because he doesn't even support his own parents.}}
## {{n-g|Used in the {{m|zh|[[再]]……也……}} concessive constructions.}} [[still]], [[anyway]], [[nevertheless]]
##: {{zh-x|你 再 聰明，也 回答 不了{liǎo} 這 個 問題。|No matter how smart you are, you won't be able to answer this question.}}
