# {{lb|zh|contemporary|_|Shanghainese Wu}} {{n-g|Used to indicate the present tense.}}

======Synonyms======
{{zh-dial}}

======Usage notes======
* {{sense|perfective aspect particle}} Most of the time, {{lang|zh|了}} is translated by a [[past tense]]. But it can also indicate that one action is completed before another.
*: {{zh-x|你 吃 了 以後 叫 我。|Call me when you are done eating.}}
* {{sense|change of state particle}} When used as the ''change of state particle'', {{lang|zh|了}} can be translated by “[[now]]”, “[[already]]” or “not [[anymore]]”.
*: {{zh-x|我 會 說 中文 了。|I can speak Chinese '''now'''. (I couldn't before.)}}
*: {{zh-x|我 喝醉 了。|I'm drunk.}}
*: {{zh-x|沒有 紙 了。|There's no paper '''anymore'''.}}
* In a question, {{lang|zh|了}} is put before the particle {{zh-l|嗎}}.
* {{q|Northern Wu}}: In [[w:Shanghainese|Shanghainese]], this term is primarily used to indicate the present ''tense'' and secondarily the perfective ''aspect''. The present tense sense is derived from Old Shanghainese {{zh-l|哉|tr=-}}. For the usage difference between other perfectives, see [[脫了#Usage notes]].
* {{q|Malaysian Mandarin|Singaporean Mandarin}}: {{zh-l|了}} is often colloquially pronounced as {{zh-l|了|liǎo}} in all instances.
*: {{zh-x|你 打掃 了{liǎo} 再 幫 我 煮飯。|Help me cook after you're done cleaning up.|M-MY}}

