=====Usage notes=====
* {{sense|personal pronoun}}
** Originally gender-neutral before the 1910s, when the character {{zh-l|她|she; her}} was coined; now usually refers to males (also occasionally refers to females).
*** However, {{zh-l|他/她/牠/它/祂}} is only a written distinction; they are all still pronounced as ''tā''.
** This term can refer to a person of unknown gender or there is no need to mention gender of the person referred to, while {{zh-l|[[他/她]]}} {{q|[[gender binary]]}} is also used; see also Internet slang {{zh-l|TA|they (singular)}}.

